Host build only — the firmware never marks the throttle calibrated.

TorqueEncoder_update() forces travelPercent = 0 while me->calibrated is
FALSE. The on-car calibration routine (Eco button held 3 s -> calibrateTPS)
is commented out in main.c, and the four tps*_calib* bounds main.c declares
at lines 218-221 are never handed to the TorqueEncoder. In the SIL harness
there is no button to hold, so the pedal the sim feeds in is thrown away
and every current command is 0 A.

Pre-load those same bounds and set calibrated = TRUE in TorqueEncoder_new().
Ask the VCU team how the car gets a calibrated pedal today; if the answer
is "a calibration routine", this patch goes away once the harness can
drive that routine instead.

--- a/torqueEncoder.c	2026-09-05 15:57:19
+++ b/torqueEncoder.c	2026-09-05 15:57:19
@@ -36,7 +36,14 @@
     me->tps1->specMin = 2500; // Target 0% = ~2650
     me->tps1->specMax = 4900; // Target 100% = ~4700
 
-    me->calibrated = FALSE;
+    // SIL: the calibration routine and its button are commented out in
+    // main.c, so nothing ever sets calibrated = TRUE and travelPercent is
+    // forced to 0. Pre-load the bounds main.c declares (and never uses).
+    me->tps0_calibMin = 400;
+    me->tps0_calibMax = 1400;
+    me->tps1_calibMin = 1800;
+    me->tps1_calibMax = 4000;
+    me->calibrated = TRUE;
 
     return me;
 }
